<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Soares da Costa profit drops - analysts.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Soares da Costa profit drops - analysts.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese construction company Soares da Costa registered a sharp profit drop in 1996, with net profit falling to 305 million escudos from 1.59 billion the year before, according to figures sent by the company to analysts.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the company refused to comment beyond saying that Soares da Costa planned to hold a news conference soon to publish its results.</p>
<p>According to the information sent to analysts, a copy of which was obtained by Reuters, the results were as follows:</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit			0.305  vs	1.590</p>
<p>Turnover			 72.835  vs     95.819</p>
<p>Profit including minorities 0.302  vs	1.594</p>
<p>Operating profit		1.096  vs	3.994</p>
<p>Liquid assets		  94.017  vs     86.040</p>
<p>Liabilities		    70.943  vs     61.814</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113125</p>
</text>
